      "nets": ["Display_Power_Switch", "GND"],
      "observed": "On the EPD_Driver sheet, C1 (the input/decoupling capacitor on the Display_Power_Switch rail, in parallel with C2) is drawn with value 0.1 uF / 16 V.",
      "expected": "The specification's component-mapping table states that the Meshinger schematic's C1 belongs to the 'C2 default' group and must be 1 uF / 25 V (the other members of that listed group, C5/C7/C8/C9/C10, are all correctly 1 uF/25 V on the sheet, isolating C1 as the single deviation).",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "C2 default: 1 µF/25 V | C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V | Matches default (EPD_Driver.kicad_sch, §4 table)"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "C1 0.1uF/16V (EPD_Driver sheet, left side, between Display_Power_Switch and GND)"}
      ],
      "impact": "C1 provides bulk decoupling on the rail that feeds the EPD boost converter (L1/Q1) and the panel VDD/VDDIO. Dropping it from 1 uF to 0.1 uF reduces the charge reservoir available during the boost converter's current bursts, which can cause the Display_Power_Switch rail to droop and produce display-refresh glitches or unstable boost operation relative to the intended design.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "All component identities and the boost/passive values (L1=10uH, R1=0.47, Q1, U1-U3, J1, C2=1uF/6.3V, and the rest of the 1uF/25V group) match the specification, but C1 on the EPD_Driver sheet is 0.1uF/16V where the spec lists it as 1uF/25V, a single value deviation within an otherwise-correct group, so I report one wrong_value anomaly."
}

